#pitfall[
  The SR decoder bounds the inner dimension by #const("MaxMixPeers")
  $= 512$, and the encoder refuses (with the error "too many mixing peers")
  to serialize an SR whose first row is longer than 512, although that
  dimension is the session's total message count $M$, which the client
  allows up to #const("MaxMtot") $= 1024$ (@sec:mixing-sizelimits) and the
  mixpool accepts up to 1024. In a session with $M > 512$, an SR is
  therefore accepted into the sender's own mixpool but cannot be written to
  any connection: a dcrd node that tries to send it closes that connection
  after the encoding error. An SR with such a width built by other software
  fails to decode at a dcrd receiver, which bans the sender for a malformed
  wire message. The reference client does not keep $M$ at or below 512 when
  forming sessions. Clients #SHOULDNOT form sessions with $M > 512$.
  #src("wire/msgmixslotreserve.go", "BtcDecode", "writeMessageNoSignature") |
  #src("peer/peer.go", "outHandler") | #src("server.go", "OnRead")
]

