=== Size limits <sec:mixing-sizelimits>

When all KEs of a session have arrived and agreement has not yet been
recorded in the epoch (agreement recorded because an alternate session
reproduced the current attempt, @sec:mixing-agreement, skips this check),
each peer checks the session against the mixing limits of
@tab:mixing-limits, walking the PRs in unmixed order and excluding a PR if
adding it would exceed 64 peers, a total of 1024 messages, or an estimated
CoinJoin size of 100000 bytes. The size estimate is
$12 + 2 dot "varintlen"(n_"in") + "varintlen"(n_"out") + 166 n_"in" + sum_"outputs" (10 + "varintlen"(ell) + ell)$
over all inputs and outputs so far, with $ell = 25$ for each mixed output and
the actual script length for each change output; a PR is excluded when the
estimate is $>= 100000$. If any PR is excluded, the remaining PRs form a new
session (@alg:mixing-sid) and the run restarts with it, provided at least
four remain. #src("mixing/mixclient/client.go", "run", "coinjoinSize.join")

=== Runs and reruns <sec:mixing-reruns>

CoinShuffle++ numbers successive runs of a session. In dcrd every run is
instead a fresh session: whenever peers are excluded (blame, timeout, size
limits, disagreement), the remaining PRs are re-sorted with
@alg:mixing-sid using the *same epoch value*, giving a new session ID, and
every message of the new attempt carries run number 0. Relays reject any
message whose run number is not 0. The `Epoch` field of every KE in the
epoch is the original epoch value, and relays accept KEs only up to
20 minutes after it (@sec:mixing-mixpool-accept), which bounds the time
available for reruns.

== The Protocol Run <sec:mixing-run>

This section describes one run of a session with peers $0 .. n - 1$ in
unmixed order. "Peer $k$" refers to unmixed positions, "message $g$" to
global message indices.

=== Deadlines <sec:mixing-deadlines>

Each run has a start time $T_0$: the epoch boundary for the first attempt
of an epoch, and the current time when a rerun is started. All deadlines
are relative to it:

#figure(
  caption: [Stage deadlines of a run ($tau$ = 30 s on the main, simulation and regression networks, 10 s on the test network)],
  table(
    columns: (auto, auto, 1fr),
    table.header([Deadline], [Time], [By then]),
    [KE], [$T_0 + tau$], [All KEs of the session received.],
    [CT], [$T_0 + 2 tau$], [All CTs received.],
    [SR], [$T_0 + 3 tau$], [All SRs received. (A peer that cannot solve roots starts waiting for a valid FP as soon as it has all SRs; @sec:mixing-roots.)],
    [DC], [$T_0 + 4 tau$], [All DCs (and FPs, sent together with them) received.],
    [DC-RS], [$T_0 + 5 tau$], [Wait for secrets revealed after the DC stage; CMs are not sent before this time.],
    [CM], [$T_0 + 6 tau$], [All CMs received.],
  ),
) <tab:mixing-deadlines>

#src("mixing/mixclient/client.go", "deadlines.start", "timeoutDuration")

#figure(
  caption: [Stages of one run. Each band names the messages that are due by
    the deadline at its right edge (@tab:mixing-deadlines).],
