Other rejections (wrong run number, expiry out of range, unknown script
class, an unconfirmed or spent UTXO, conflicting messages, invalid session
order, and so on) are not bannable. The source notes for several of them
that a peer may relay such a message in good faith, for example a KE whose
PRs it does not know.

=== Orphans <sec:mixing-orphans>

The orphan pool holds at most 250 messages. When adding an orphan would
exceed that, the node counts orphans per source peer and removes orphans of
the source with the most orphans, then of the next, and so on (from each
source as many as are needed, up to all of them), until 187 remain; the new
orphan is then added. When a PR is
accepted, orphan KEs of that identity that reference it are reconsidered;
when a KE is accepted, the identity's orphans in that session are accepted.
Orphans are removed 20 minutes after they were stored, orphan KEs also when
their epoch is more than 20 minutes old, and all orphans of an identity when
its PR is removed. #src("mixing/mixpool/mixpool.go", "addOrphan", "limitNumOrphans", "reconsiderOrphans")

=== Expiry and removal <sec:mixing-mixpool-expiry>

When a block extends the main chain, dcrd removes from the mixpool the
session of any transaction in the block that is a known completed mix, and
every PR with an outpoint spent by any other transaction in the block,
together with all messages of that identity and the sessions they took part
in. It also schedules expiry: after waiting until the second epoch boundary
from now, it removes every session whose expiry is at or below the height
recorded when the wait began, and every PR whose `Expiry` is at or below it.
#src("mixing/mixpool/mixpool.go", "RemoveSpentPRs", "ExpireMessagesInBackground", "expireMessagesNow")

=== Interaction with the mempool and voting <sec:mixing-observer>

Two further policies protect mixes from disruption (they belong to
#chref("policy") but are driven by the mixpool):

- The mempool rejects a transaction that spends an outpoint of a current
  pair request unless it is the completed mix of a known session.
- The mixpool _observer_ examines, at each epoch boundary, the previous
  epoch. Among sessions of at least four KEs that reached the CT stage and
  revealed no secrets, a session is complete if every peer sent a CM. An
  identity that sent a KE and a CT in some session of a pairing but was not
  in a completed mix receives a _strike_ if a mix of that pairing completed;
  if none completed, it receives a strike only if it was one of the peers
  whose message was missing at the first incomplete stage of a session in
  which all KEs were present. Strikes are recorded against the identity's
  PR outpoints (merged with any strike set sharing an outpoint), removed
  for the PR outpoints of the peers of a session found complete and for the
  inputs of a known mix transaction contained in a block, and forgotten
  once the latest strike is at least 24 hours older than the epoch being
  examined. Outputs with two or more strikes
  (#const("strikeLimit")) cause the client to exclude PRs spending them, the
  mempool to reject non-mix transactions spending them, and dcrd not to
  announce the winning tickets of a block containing such a spend, so that
  its voting wallets do not vote on that block.

#src("mixing/mixpool/observer.go", "checkPrevEpoch", "updateStrikes", "MisbehavingBlock") |
#src("internal/mempool/mempool.go", "maybeAcceptTransaction")

